{"OS":{"id":"c23cca3b-9027-48f0-807c-e57e50135f20","word":"OS","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"operating system","word":"SO"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"We've got an OS of the Cuckmere area.","bold_text_offsets":[[13,15]],"type":"example","id":"a691fd78-e410-4b67-b70d-d8c4a4b7cc76"},{"text":"Calton Hill in Edinburgh is located at OS grid ref NT262741.","bold_text_offsets":[[39,41]],"type":"example","id":"2bebc6a8-d8bb-46aa-9680-4754cab66296"}],"categories":["British English","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["Ordnance Survey","Ordnance Survey"]],"raw_glosses":["(UK) An Ordnance Survey map."],"glosses":["An Ordnance Survey map."],"tags":["UK"],"id":"af46586b-7391-4f31-831d-27ed3ea6aa26"},{"examples":[{"text":"I've decided to install two different OSes on my new laptop.","bold_text_offsets":[[38,42]],"type":"example","id":"ab1676a5-5aa1-44ec-83dd-3633ee2ed28d"},{"text":"Some vendors do now have a variant of the per-unit royalty (usually termed a “shared risk,” or similar approach), but it is not strictly the same as for those proprietary embedded OSes mentioned before […]","ref":"2008, Karim Yaghmour, Jon Masters, Gilad Ben-Yossef, Building Embedded Linux Systems:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[180,184]],"id":"7799eddb-9f5c-4d78-ae30-620982d899b7"},{"text":"A policy-created scheduled task will be accepted by computers running client OSes as old as Windows 2000 […]","ref":"2010, Jorge Orchilles, Microsoft Windows 7 Administrator's Reference:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[77,81]],"id":"68383d2e-7aba-453d-a3fb-904e1d04fb57"},{"text":"In a dual-boot configuration, you install two OSs on the computer (Windows XP and Windows 2000, for example).","ref":"2009, Emmett Dulaney, CompTIA A+ Complete Review Guide:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[46,49]],"id":"d02c0d6f-fcbc-4076-bcb6-90f797ec5824"}],"topics":["computing","engineering","mathematics","natural-sciences","ph